course: dictionary
lesson: 1215
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Important trips need a buffer, spare time in case something goes wrong.» Here a buffer is extra time kept spare, so the clue is spare time and something going wrong.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «A buffer is extra time kept spare in case something goes wrong, such as a lost passport or traffic.» Spare time fits, so your meaning works. A word can also change its form: buffer is a thing (a noun), while buffering is an action (a verb).
explain: Check the topic too. A train buffer, a video buffer and a science buffer are different meanings of the same word, and the subject of the text shows you which one is meant.
fact: A buffer is something that protects one thing from another, or softens a hit or shock.
fact: On a train track, buffers are springs or pads at the end of the line that soften a crash.
fact: In computing, a buffer stores data for a short time, and «buffering» is when a video waits to load.
fact: In science, a buffer is a solution that keeps acidity (pH) from changing much.
fact: «An old buffer» is informal UK slang for an old-fashioned man, often silly.
exercise: «Important trips need a buffer, spare time in case something goes wrong.» What is a buffer here? | A video that has stopped | A kind of train | A rude old man | * Spare time kept in case something goes wrong
exercise: «The video keeps stopping and saying buffering.» What does buffering mean? | The video is being painted | The video is very loud | * The video is waiting to load | The video has finished playing
exercise: «The train hit the buffers at the end of the track, and the springs softened the crash.» What are the buffers here? | Spare time kept for trips | * Springs or pads that soften a crash | A rude person | A kind of video
test: Grandad calls the man next door «an old buffer». What does he mean? | A very fast runner | A man who protects people from danger | A liquid used in a science lab | * An old-fashioned man, often silly
test: In science, a buffer keeps what from changing much? | * Acidity (pH) | The size of a room | The weather | The time on a clock
exam: Which phrase means a space that keeps two areas apart? | Spare time | * Buffer zone | Buffering video | Old buffer
